# ElixirOffice environment (copy to .env, never commit .env).
#
# Elixir AI is OFF unless configured. Two ways to enable it:
#  1. Server (this file): every user gets AI without a key in the browser (docs/ai.md, make ai-proxy / make ai-check).
#  2. Each user, in File > AI, with their own service and key (stored only in their browser).
#
# Any OpenAI-compatible endpoint: OpenAI, Mistral, Ollama, vLLM, an internal gateway.
#ELIXIR_AI_BASE_URL=https://api.openai.com/v1
#ELIXIR_AI_MODEL=gpt-4.1-mini
#ELIXIR_AI_API_KEY=
# Examples:
#   Mistral : ELIXIR_AI_BASE_URL=https://api.mistral.ai/v1   ELIXIR_AI_MODEL=mistral-small-latest
#   Ollama  : ELIXIR_AI_BASE_URL=http://host.docker.internal:11434/v1   ELIXIR_AI_MODEL=llama3.1  (no key)
#   vLLM    : ELIXIR_AI_BASE_URL=https://vllm.example.org/v1   ELIXIR_AI_MODEL=<served model name>
# Legacy: OPENAI_API_KEY alone means OpenAI with gpt-4.1-mini.

# Optional private CA certificates for the AI HTTPS upstream (path inside the container).
# EO_AI_CA_FILE=/etc/elixiroffice/ai-ca.pem
